title: AutoGen kind()/apiVersion() setter is a silent no-op on generated classes
updated: 2026-08-27T18:48:20Z
---

lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen.pm:192 -- top-level schemas carry a kind property,
which becomes a rw Moo attribute; add_symbol("&kind", sub { $kind_val })
then overwrites the accessor. $obj->kind("Other") silently returns the
GVK constant and the write vanishes.

Repro (measured): on a generated class, kind("Other") returns the
original Kind, unchanged, no error.

Output stays correct; only the write path lies. Fix sketch: skip
kind/apiVersion when generating property attributes for classes that get
GVK methods installed -- same line as karr #45 took for the hand-written
template classes.

Found in the 2026-08-18 core-module review (repro verified).
Lane: io-k8s-worker, then io-k8s-test-writer (t/04_autogen.t).

Fixed: apiVersion/kind/metadata properties are skipped for classes receiving GVK class methods (karr #45 line). Found the worse half in passing: apiVersion had no accessor collision, so it stayed writable and overwrote the role-supplied value -- a manifest could claim a foreign GVK. Tests: t/57_autogen_karr_55_60.t.
